        "source_span": {
          "end_page": 3,
          "end_text": "partof the cognitiveprocess.Cognitiveprocessesain't(all)in the head!",
          "start_page": 2,
          "start_text": "Wheredoesthemindstopandtherestof theworldbegin?"
        },
        "summary": "The paper asks where the mind stops, reviews standard replies, and proposes active externalism. It uses three problem-solving cases and Tetris to introduce the parity principle and epistemic action.",
        "title": "Extended Cognition and the Parity Principle"
      },
      {
        "pages": {
          "end": 7,
          "start": 4
        },
        "source_span": {
          "end_page": 7,
          "end_text": "extendedcognitionis a corecognitiveprocess, not anadd-onextra.",
          "start_page": 4,
          "start_text": "This externalism differs from the standard variety advocated by Putnam"
        },
        "summary": "Defines cognitive extension as a two-way coupled system, contrasts active externalism with passive externalism, and answers portability/Naked Mind objections via reliable coupling, evolution, and language.",
        "title": "Active Externalism, Coupling, and Objections"
      },
      {
        "pages": {
          "end": 9,
          "start": 7
        },
        "source_span": {
          "end_page": 9,
          "end_text": "a beliefis simplynotinthehead.",
          "start_page": 7,
          "start_text": "So far we have spoken largely about 'cognitiveprocessing'"
        },
        "summary": "Moves from cognition to mind by arguing that beliefs can be partly constituted by environmental features. The Otto/Inga analogy, Twin Otto, and the notebook example show belief roles can be realized outside the head.",
        "title": "Extended Belief: Otto and Inga"
      },
      {
        "pages": {
          "end": 13,
          "start": 10
        },
        "source_span": {
          "end_page": 13,
          "end_text": "Language, thus construed, is not a mirrorof ourinnerstatesbut a complementto them.",
          "start_page": 10,
          "start_text": "It might be suggested that the cases are relevante different"
        },
        "summary": "Addresses objections about reliability, access, and phenomenology; lists features of extended belief; discusses puzzle cases, the Internet, social extension, and language as a tool for spreading cognition.",
        "title": "Criteria, Puzzle Cases, and Social Extension"
      },
      {
        "pages": {
          "end": 13,
          "start": 13
        },
        "source_span": {
          "end_page": 13,
          "end_text": "we may be ableto see ourselvesmoretrulyas creaturesof the world.",
          "start_page": 13,
          "start_text": "What, finally, of the self?"
        },
        "summary": "Extends the argument to the self: Otto is an extended system, and the view has moral and social consequences when environments become part of persons.",
        "title": "Extended Self and Ethical Consequences"
      },
